{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"10153","self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/latest/issue/10153","key":"AP-29","fields":{"summary":"enable fractional duration","issuetype":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issuetype/10037","id":"10037","description":"Stories track functionality or features expressed as user goals.","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10315?size=medium","name":"Story","subtask":false,"avatarId":10315,"entityId":"a9502e0d-867b-4e13-9c45-261e65fe910f","hierarchyLevel":0},"parent":{"id":"10033","key":"AP-1","self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/10033","fields":{"summary":"Core Scheduling Engine MVP","status":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/status/10066","description":"","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/","name":"To Do","id":"10066","statusCategory":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/statuscategory/2","id":2,"key":"new","colorName":"blue-gray","name":"To Do"}},"priority":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/priority/1","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/images/icons/priorities/highest_new.svg","name":"Highest","id":"1"},"issuetype":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issuetype/10035","id":"10035","description":"Epics track collections of related bugs, stories, and tasks.","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10307?size=medium","name":"Epic","subtask":false,"avatarId":10307,"entityId":"21b28705-2e2b-43f3-95af-c2d445b6d5a2","hierarchyLevel":1}}},"creator":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/user?accountId=712020%3Aef0c8c11-3cf2-4fc0-97ac-2cdbf24d876c","accountId":"712020:ef0c8c11-3cf2-4fc0-97ac-2cdbf24d876c","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png"},"displayName":"KidBlend App ","active":true,"timeZone":"Europe/Minsk","accountType":"atlassian"},"components":[],"created":"2025-12-17T06:25:23.423+0300","description":"## Overview\r\n\r\n**Purpose**: This solution design document provides a structured approach for enhancing the schedule calculator to support fractional durations with working days calculation, enabling accurate scheduling for tasks with partial day estimates.\r\n\r\n**Usage**: This design breaks down the technical requirements for implementing fractional duration support with working days (Monday-Friday) and configurable non-working days, while maintaining backward compatibility with existing functionality.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Business Context\r\n\r\n### Problem Statement\r\n\r\nThe current schedule calculator treats all days as working days and doesn't properly handle fractional durations (e.g., 3.5 days). When calculating completion dates, fractional durations are rounded to whole days without considering working days (Monday-Friday) or configurable holidays. This leads to inaccurate schedule predictions, especially for tasks that don't require full days of work.\r\n\r\n### Business Objectives\r\n\r\n**Objective 1**: Enable accurate scheduling with fractional duration estimates (e.g., 2.5 days, 3.5 days) to support more precise task planning.\r\n\r\n**Objective 2**: Implement working days calculation that excludes weekends (Saturday and Sunday) and configurable non-working days (holidays) from schedule calculations.\r\n\r\n**Objective 3**: Ensure completion dates are properly rounded up to the next working day when fractional durations result in partial day completion.\r\n\r\n### Success Criteria\r\n\r\n**Criterion 1**: Tasks with fractional durations (e.g., 2.5 days) starting on Monday complete on Wednesday (rounded up), not Tuesday.\r\n\r\n**Criterion 2**: Tasks spanning weekends properly skip Saturday and Sunday in date calculations (e.g., task starting Friday with 1.5 days duration completes on Monday).\r\n\r\n**Criterion 3**: Configuration supports additional non-working days (holidays) that are excluded from working days calculations.\r\n\r\n**Criterion 4**: Sequential tasks properly chain start/end dates with no gaps or overlaps in working days.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Solution Architecture\r\n\r\n### High-Level Architecture\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\ngraph TB\r\n    subgraph \"Input Layer\"\r\n        A[CSV Parser]\r\n        B[Config Loader]\r\n    end\r\n    subgraph \"Processing Layer\"\r\n        C[Working Days Calculator]\r\n        D[Duration Calculator]\r\n        E[Schedule Calculator]\r\n    end\r\n    subgraph \"Output Layer\"\r\n        F[JSON Output Generator]\r\n    end\r\n    A --> E\r\n    B --> C\r\n    B --> E\r\n    C --> E\r\n    D --> E\r\n    E --> F\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Description**: The enhanced architecture introduces a Working Days Calculator component that processes non-working days configuration and provides working day arithmetic. The Duration Calculator continues to support fractional durations, while the Schedule Calculator orchestrates sequential task scheduling using working days logic. The Config Loader now handles non-working days configuration.\r\n\r\n### Component Architecture\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\nflowchart TD\r\n    Start([Task List + Config]) --> Parse{Parse Config}\r\n    Parse -->|Success| Validate{Validate Config}\r\n    Parse -->|Error| Error[Handle Error]\r\n    Validate -->|Valid| InitWorkingDays[Initialize Working Days Calendar]\r\n    Validate -->|Invalid| Error\r\n    InitWorkingDays --> ProcessTasks[Process Tasks Sequentially]\r\n    ProcessTasks --> CalcDuration[Calculate Duration]\r\n    CalcDuration --> CalcWorkingDays[Calculate Working Days]\r\n    CalcWorkingDays --> RoundUp{Round Up Completion Date}\r\n    RoundUp --> NextWorkingDay[Move to Next Working Day]\r\n    NextWorkingDay --> UpdateSchedule[Update Schedule]\r\n    UpdateSchedule --> MoreTasks{More Tasks?}\r\n    MoreTasks -->|Yes| ProcessTasks\r\n    MoreTasks -->|No| GenerateOutput[Generate Output]\r\n    GenerateOutput --> End([Scheduled Tasks])\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Description**: The workflow processes tasks sequentially, calculating fractional durations, converting to working days, rounding up completion dates, and ensuring dates fall on working days. The working days calendar is initialized from configuration (default weekends + custom holidays).\r\n\r\n### Data Architecture\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\nerDiagram\r\n    TASK ||--o{ SCHEDULED_TASK : \"scheduled as\"\r\n    CONFIG ||--|| WORKING_DAYS_CALENDAR : \"defines\"\r\n    SCHEDULED_TASK }o--|| WORKING_DAYS_CALENDAR : \"uses\"\r\n    \r\n    TASK {\r\n        string id PK\r\n        string title\r\n        number estimate\r\n        string component\r\n        string parentId\r\n        string issueType\r\n    }\r\n    \r\n    SCHEDULED_TASK {\r\n        string id PK\r\n        string calculatedStartDate\r\n        string calculatedEndDate\r\n        number duration\r\n    }\r\n    \r\n    CONFIG {\r\n        string projectStartDate\r\n        number sprintDurationDays\r\n        number velocity\r\n        array nonWorkingDays\r\n    }\r\n    \r\n    WORKING_DAYS_CALENDAR {\r\n        set nonWorkingDays\r\n        function isWorkingDay\r\n        function addWorkingDays\r\n        function nextWorkingDay\r\n    }\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Description**: The data model extends the existing Task and ScheduledTask interfaces. The ScheduleConfig interface is enhanced with a `nonWorkingDays` array. A WorkingDaysCalendar component manages working day calculations, providing methods to check if a date is a working day, add working days to a date, and find the next working day.\r\n\r\n### Integration Architecture\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\nsequenceDiagram\r\n    participant CLI\r\n    participant ConfigLoader\r\n    participant WorkingDaysCalculator\r\n    participant ScheduleCalculator\r\n    participant OutputGenerator\r\n    \r\n    CLI->>ConfigLoader: Load config.json\r\n    ConfigLoader->>ConfigLoader: Validate config\r\n    ConfigLoader->>WorkingDaysCalculator: Initialize calendar\r\n    WorkingDaysCalculator->>WorkingDaysCalculator: Build non-working days set\r\n    CLI->>ScheduleCalculator: Calculate schedule(tasks, config)\r\n    ScheduleCalculator->>ScheduleCalculator: For each task sequentially\r\n    ScheduleCalculator->>ScheduleCalculator: Calculate fractional duration\r\n    ScheduleCalculator->>WorkingDaysCalculator: Add working days(startDate, duration)\r\n    WorkingDaysCalculator->>WorkingDaysCalculator: Round up to next working day\r\n    WorkingDaysCalculator-->>ScheduleCalculator: Return completion date\r\n    ScheduleCalculator->>ScheduleCalculator: Update current date\r\n    ScheduleCalculator-->>CLI: Return scheduled tasks\r\n    CLI->>OutputGenerator: Generate output.json\r\n    OutputGenerator-->>CLI: Output file created\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Description**: The sequence shows the enhanced workflow where the WorkingDaysCalculator is initialized from configuration and used by the ScheduleCalculator to compute working day-based completion dates. Each task's completion date is calculated using working days arithmetic, ensuring weekends and holidays are skipped.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Technical Design\r\n\r\n### Technology Stack\r\n\r\n**Runtime & Language:**\r\n- Node.js - Runtime environment\r\n- TypeScript - Type-safe development\r\n\r\n**Libraries & Frameworks:**\r\n- No external date libraries required - Native JavaScript Date API with custom working days logic\r\n\r\n**Tools & Infrastructure:**\r\n- Vitest - Unit testing framework\r\n- TypeScript Compiler - Type checking and compilation\r\n\r\n### Design Patterns\r\n\r\n**Pattern 1: Strategy Pattern** - Working days calculation strategy can be extended to support different work week configurations (e.g., 4-day work weeks, custom schedules).\r\n\r\n**Pattern 2: Calendar Abstraction** - WorkingDaysCalendar encapsulates all working day logic, making it testable and maintainable.\r\n\r\n**Pattern 3: Immutable Configuration** - ScheduleConfig remains immutable after initialization, ensuring consistent behavior throughout the application lifecycle.\r\n\r\n### Security Considerations\r\n\r\n**Security measure 1**: Input validation for date formats prevents injection attacks through malformed date strings.\r\n\r\n**Security measure 2**: Configuration validation ensures non-working days array contains valid ISO date strings only.\r\n\r\n**Security measure 3**: Type checking prevents runtime errors from invalid data types.\r\n\r\n### Performance Considerations\r\n\r\n**Performance optimization 1**: Working days calendar is initialized once and cached, avoiding repeated calculations for each task.\r\n\r\n**Performance optimization 2**: Non-working days are stored in a Set data structure for O(1) lookup performance.\r\n\r\n**Performance optimization 3**: Working days calculation uses efficient date arithmetic without iterating through all dates.\r\n\r\n### Scalability Considerations\r\n\r\n**Scalability approach 1**: The working days calculator can handle large numbers of non-working days (holidays) efficiently using Set-based lookups.\r\n\r\n**Scalability approach 2**: Sequential task processing maintains O(n) complexity where n is the number of tasks.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Development Scope Decomposition\r\n\r\n### Decomposition Strategy\r\n\r\n**Approach: Single Solution Design**\r\n\r\nThe scope is manageable as a single implementation. The enhancement involves:\r\n- Extending configuration to support non-working days\r\n- Creating a working days calculator component\r\n- Enhancing the schedule calculator to use working days logic\r\n- Updating date arithmetic to round up completion dates\r\n\r\nThese components are tightly coupled and should be developed together to ensure consistency.\r\n\r\n### Component 1: Working Days Calculator\r\n\r\n**Scope**: Core component for working days calculation logic, including weekend exclusion, holiday support, and date arithmetic.\r\n\r\n**Task 1.1: Create WorkingDaysCalendar class**\r\n\r\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\r\n- * AC1: Class provides `isWorkingDay(date: string): boolean` method that returns true for Monday-Friday, false for Saturday-Sunday and configured holidays\r\n- * AC2: Class provides `addWorkingDays(startDate: string, days: number): string` method that adds fractional working days and rounds up to next working day\r\n- * AC3: Class provides `nextWorkingDay(date: string): string` method that returns the next working day from a given date\r\n- * AC4: Class initializes with default weekends (Saturday, Sunday) and optional non-working days array from configuration\r\n- * AC5: Non-working days are stored in a Set for efficient O(1) lookup\r\n\r\n**Dependencies**: None (foundational component)\r\n\r\n**Estimated Effort**: 3 story points\r\n\r\n**Task 1.2: Implement working days arithmetic with rounding**\r\n\r\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\r\n- * AC1: `addWorkingDays()` correctly handles fractional durations (e.g., 2.5 days starting Monday → Wednesday)\r\n- * AC2: `addWorkingDays()` rounds up partial day completions to the next working day\r\n- * AC3: `addWorkingDays()` skips weekends when calculating working days\r\n- * AC4: `addWorkingDays()` skips configured holidays when calculating working days\r\n- * AC5: Edge case: task starting Friday with 1.5 days → completes Monday (skips weekend)\r\n\r\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1\r\n\r\n**Estimated Effort**: 5 story points\r\n\r\n### Component 2: Configuration Enhancement\r\n\r\n**Scope**: Extend schedule configuration to support non-working days array and update validation logic.\r\n\r\n**Task 2.1: Extend ScheduleConfig interface and types**\r\n\r\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\r\n- * AC1: `ScheduleConfig` interface includes optional `nonWorkingDays?: string[]` field\r\n- * AC2: `nonWorkingDays` array contains ISO date strings (YYYY-MM-DD format)\r\n- * AC3: `RawScheduleConfig` interface includes optional `nonWorkingDays?: unknown` field\r\n- * AC4: Configuration types are backward compatible (nonWorkingDays is optional)\r\n\r\n**Dependencies**: None\r\n\r\n**Estimated Effort**: 1 story point\r\n\r\n**Task 2.2: Update configuration validator**\r\n\r\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\r\n- * AC1: Validator accepts optional `nonWorkingDays` array in configuration\r\n- * AC2: Validator validates each date in `nonWorkingDays` array is a valid ISO date string (YYYY-MM-DD)\r\n- * AC3: Validator rejects invalid date formats in `nonWorkingDays` array with clear error messages\r\n- * AC4: Validator allows empty array or undefined for `nonWorkingDays` (defaults to weekends only)\r\n- * AC5: Validation errors clearly indicate which dates in the array are invalid\r\n\r\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.1\r\n\r\n**Estimated Effort**: 3 story points\r\n\r\n### Component 3: Schedule Calculator Enhancement\r\n\r\n**Scope**: Integrate working days calculator into schedule calculation logic, replacing simple date arithmetic.\r\n\r\n**Task 3.1: Integrate WorkingDaysCalendar into schedule calculator**\r\n\r\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\r\n- * AC1: Schedule calculator initializes WorkingDaysCalendar from configuration\r\n- * AC2: `addDays()` function is replaced with `workingDaysCalendar.addWorkingDays()` for date calculations\r\n- * AC3: Duration calculations continue to support fractional values (e.g., 2.5, 3.5 days)\r\n- * AC4: Completion dates are calculated using working days, excluding weekends and holidays\r\n- * AC5: Sequential tasks properly chain: each task starts on the previous task's completion date\r\n\r\n**Dependencies**: Component 1 (Working Days Calculator), Component 2 (Configuration Enhancement)\r\n\r\n**Estimated Effort**: 5 story points\r\n\r\n**Task 3.2: Update schedule calculator to preserve fractional durations**\r\n\r\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\r\n- * AC1: Duration values remain fractional in calculations (e.g., 2.5 days stored as 2.5, not rounded to 3)\r\n- * AC2: Start and finish dates are always whole days in ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD)\r\n- * AC3: Completion date rounding logic applies only to final dates, not intermediate calculations\r\n- * AC4: Example: Task with 2.5 days starting Monday → duration=2.5, startDate=Monday, endDate=Wednesday\r\n\r\n**Dependencies**: Task 3.1\r\n\r\n**Estimated Effort**: 2 story points\r\n\r\n### Component 4: Testing and Validation\r\n\r\n**Scope**: Comprehensive unit tests covering fractional durations, working days, rounding logic, and edge cases.\r\n\r\n**Task 4.1: Unit tests for WorkingDaysCalendar**\r\n\r\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\r\n- * AC1: Tests verify `isWorkingDay()` correctly identifies Monday-Friday as working days\r\n- * AC2: Tests verify `isWorkingDay()` correctly identifies Saturday-Sunday as non-working days\r\n- * AC3: Tests verify `isWorkingDay()` correctly identifies configured holidays as non-working days\r\n- * AC4: Tests verify `addWorkingDays()` with fractional durations (2.5 days) rounds up correctly\r\n- * AC5: Tests verify `addWorkingDays()` skips weekends (e.g., Friday + 1.5 days → Monday)\r\n- * AC6: Tests verify `addWorkingDays()` skips configured holidays\r\n- * AC7: Tests verify `nextWorkingDay()` returns next working day, skipping weekends and holidays\r\n\r\n**Dependencies**: Component 1\r\n\r\n**Estimated Effort**: 5 story points\r\n\r\n**Task 4.2: Integration tests for schedule calculator with working days**\r\n\r\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\r\n- * AC1: Test: Task with 2.5 days starting Monday → completes Wednesday (rounded up)\r\n- * AC2: Test: Two tasks each 2.5 days starting Monday → first finishes Wednesday, second starts Wednesday and finishes Friday\r\n- * AC3: Test: Task starting Friday with 1.5 days → completes Monday (skipping weekend, rounded up)\r\n- * AC4: Test: Task with fractional duration (3.5 days) → duration preserved as fractional, dates are whole days\r\n- * AC5: Test: Configuration with non-working days → those dates excluded from calculations\r\n- * AC6: Test: Sequential tasks → each task starts on previous task's completion date\r\n- * AC7: Test: Edge cases: tasks spanning multiple weeks, holidays, year boundaries\r\n\r\n**Dependencies**: Component 3\r\n\r\n**Estimated Effort**: 5 story points\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Development Workflow\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\ngraph LR\r\n    A[Planning] --> B[Design]\r\n    B --> C[Development]\r\n    C --> D[Code Review]\r\n    D --> E[Testing]\r\n    E --> F{Pass?}\r\n    F -->|Yes| G[Deploy]\r\n    F -->|No| C\r\n    G --> H[Monitor]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Description**: Standard development workflow with iterative testing. Development follows TDD approach where unit tests are written first for WorkingDaysCalendar, then implementation follows. Integration tests validate end-to-end functionality before code review and deployment.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Dependencies & Risks\r\n\r\n### Dependencies\r\n\r\n**External Dependency 1**: None - Solution uses native JavaScript Date API and standard TypeScript features.\r\n\r\n**Internal Dependency 1**: Existing schedule calculator and configuration system must remain backward compatible during enhancement.\r\n\r\n### Risks & Mitigation\r\n\r\n**Risk 1**: Breaking changes to existing schedule calculations when introducing working days logic.\r\n\r\n**Probability**: Medium\r\n\r\n**Impact**: High\r\n\r\n**Mitigation**: Comprehensive test coverage for existing functionality, backward compatibility validation (configurations without nonWorkingDays should work as before with weekends only), and gradual rollout with validation.\r\n\r\n**Risk 2**: Performance degradation with large numbers of non-working days (holidays) in configuration.\r\n\r\n**Probability**: Low\r\n\r\n**Impact**: Medium\r\n\r\n**Mitigation**: Use Set data structure for O(1) lookups, initialize calendar once and cache, optimize date arithmetic algorithms.\r\n\r\n**Risk 3**: Edge cases with date calculations across year boundaries, leap years, or timezone issues.\r\n\r\n**Probability**: Medium\r\n\r\n**Impact**: Medium\r\n\r\n**Mitigation**: Comprehensive edge case testing, use ISO date format consistently, validate date arithmetic with known test cases.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Testing Strategy\r\n\r\n### Unit Testing\r\n\r\n**Coverage target**: 90%+ for new WorkingDaysCalendar component and enhanced schedule calculator logic.\r\n\r\n**Key areas**: Working day identification, fractional duration arithmetic, rounding logic, weekend/holiday exclusion, date boundary cases.\r\n\r\n### Integration Testing\r\n\r\n**Scope**: End-to-end schedule calculation with various configurations (with/without holidays, different start dates, fractional durations).\r\n\r\n**Key scenarios**: \r\n- Sequential tasks with fractional durations\r\n- Tasks spanning weekends\r\n- Tasks with configured holidays\r\n- Edge cases (year boundaries, leap years)\r\n\r\n### End-to-End Testing\r\n\r\n**Scope**: Full CLI workflow from CSV input through configuration loading to schedule calculation and JSON output.\r\n\r\n**Key user journeys**: \r\n- User provides CSV with tasks and config.json with non-working days → receives accurate schedule\r\n- User provides CSV with tasks and config.json without non-working days → receives schedule with weekends only (backward compatible)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Deployment Plan\r\n\r\n### Environments\r\n\r\n**Development**: Local development with test data and configurations.\r\n\r\n**Staging**: Integration testing with sample project data.\r\n\r\n**Production**: Deployment after validation in staging environment.\r\n\r\n### Deployment Strategy\r\n\r\n**Approach**: Direct deployment with backward compatibility guarantee.\r\n\r\n**Rollback plan**: Previous version remains available, configuration changes are additive (nonWorkingDays is optional).\r\n\r\n**Monitoring**: Monitor schedule calculation accuracy, validate output against known test cases, check for performance regressions.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Documentation Requirements\r\n\r\n**API Documentation**: JSDoc comments for all new public methods in WorkingDaysCalendar and enhanced schedule calculator functions.\r\n\r\n**User Documentation**: Update README with examples of fractional duration calculations and non-working days configuration format.\r\n\r\n**Technical Documentation**: Architecture decision records for working days calculation approach and rounding strategy.\r\n\r\n**Runbooks**: None required (CLI tool, no operational runbooks needed).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Timeline & Milestones\r\n\r\n**Milestone 1**: Working Days Calculator Implementation - Week 1\r\n\r\n**Milestone 2**: Configuration Enhancement and Integration - Week 1-2\r\n\r\n**Milestone 3**: Testing and Validation - Week 2\r\n\r\n**Milestone 4**: Documentation and Deployment - Week 2\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Open Questions\r\n\r\n**Question 1**: Should the system support different work week configurations (e.g., 4-day work weeks, Tuesday-Saturday schedules)? - **Status**: Out of scope for initial implementation, can be added later via Strategy pattern.\r\n\r\n**Question 2**: How should the system handle timezone considerations for non-working days? - **Status**: Resolved - Using ISO date format (YYYY-MM-DD) without time component eliminates timezone issues.\r\n\r\n**Question 3**: Should fractional durations be displayed in output, or only whole day dates? - **Status**: Resolved - Duration values remain fractional for accuracy, but start/finish dates are always whole days per requirements.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Appendix\r\n\r\n### References\r\n\r\n**[Reference 1]**: [Solution Design Template](https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AC/pages/25133058/Solution+design+template)\r\n\r\n**[Reference 2]**: [JIRA Story Template](https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AC/pages/786465/JIRA+Template+Story)\r\n\r\n### Glossary\r\n\r\n**Working Day**: Monday through Friday, excluding weekends (Saturday, Sunday) and configured holidays.\r\n\r\n**Fractional Duration**: Duration value expressed as a decimal number (e.g., 2.5 days, 3.5 days) representing partial day estimates.\r\n\r\n**Completion Date Rounding**: Process of rounding up partial day completions to the next working day (e.g., 2.5 days starting Monday completes Wednesday, not Tuesday afternoon).\r\n\r\n**Non-Working Days**: Days excluded from schedule calculations, including default weekends (Saturday, Sunday) and optionally configured holidays.\r\n\r\n**Sequential Scheduling**: Task scheduling approach where each task starts when the previous task finishes, with no gaps or overlaps.","reporter":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/user?accountId=712020%3Aef0c8c11-3cf2-4fc0-97ac-2cdbf24d876c","accountId":"712020:ef0c8c11-3cf2-4fc0-97ac-2cdbf24d876c","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png"},"displayName":"KidBlend App ","active":true,"timeZone":"Europe/Minsk","accountType":"atlassian"},"fixVersions":[],"priority":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/priority/3","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/images/icons/priorities/medium_new.svg","name":"Medium","id":"3"},"labels":["ai_generated"],"attachment":[],"issuelinks":[],"updated":"2025-12-17T07:06:41.526+0300","status":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/status/10069","description":"","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/","name":"IN REVIEW","id":"10069","statusCategory":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/statuscategory/4","id":4,"key":"indeterminate","colorName":"yellow","name":"In Progress"}}}}],"isLast":true}